        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Mass trial of MS-13 gang at CECOT prison Americas Issued on: 24/04/2026 - 11:48 El Salvador has launched a mass trial of 486 alleged MS-13 members accused by prosecutors of thousands of murders and other crimes, as President Nayib Bukele continues his sweeping crackdown under a state of emergency that has sharply reduced crime, though human rights groups warn the measures—introduced in 2022—have led to serious abuses, including violations of due process, reports of torture, and more than 500 deaths in prison, as reported by Caroline Baum. Warner Bros. takeover by Paramount 24/04/2026 Americas Sheinbaum weighs sanctions on Chihuahua state after CIA agents died after drug lab raid in Mexico 22/04/2026 Americas 'Trump's high-stakes political theatre: US winning conventional war, Iran winning asymmetrical war' 22/04/2026 Middle East Brazil's Ava-Guarani fight for justice 21/04/2026 Americas US held secret talks with Cuba 21/04/2026 Americas US Labor Secretary Lori Chevez-Deremer leaves Trump Cabinet 21/04/2026 Americas Apple's veteran John Ternus named as new CEO 21/04/2026 Americas Victor Wembanyama unanimously named NBA Defensive Player of the Year 21/04/2026 Americas Apple's Tim Cook steps down: John Ternus names as new CEO 21/04/2026 Americas"
